.TH GROUPS 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
groups \- print the groups a user is in
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B groups
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the names of the current user's primary and supplementary groups.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH NOTES
Only the current user is supported -- \fBgroups\fR \fIUSERNAME\fR (another user) is not.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
